import './Privacy.css'; export default function Privacy() { return ( <main className="privacy-page"> <article className="privacy-content"> <header className="privacy-header"> <p className="privacy-eyebrow">SHINZI • YOUR DATA</p> <h1>Privacy Policy</h1> <p className="privacy-subtitle"> How Shinzi collects, uses, stores, and protects your information. </p> <p className="privacy-updated"> Effective date: To be announced </p> </header> <section> <h2>1. Introduction</h2> <p> Welcome to Shinzi. This Privacy Policy explains how Shinzi ("we", "our", or "us") handles information when you use our website and services. </p> <p> By using Shinzi, you acknowledge that information may be processed as described in this policy. Please read it carefully. </p> </section> <section> <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2> <p>Depending on how you use Shinzi, we may collect or process:</p> <ul> <li> <strong>Account information:</strong> Your email address and authentication information used to create and access your account. </li> <li> <strong>Profile information:</strong> Your display name, username, gender, and date of birth when provided during signup. </li> <li> <strong>Profile photo information:</strong> Your selected photo and related file information, such as its filename, file type, size, and Google Drive file reference. </li> <li> <strong>Technical information:</strong> Information that may be processed by our hosting, authentication, and database providers to operate, maintain, and secure the service. </li> </ul> <p> We aim to collect information needed to operate Shinzi and provide its features. We do not claim to collect information that the service does not actually process. </p> </section> <section> <h2>3. Date of Birth</h2> <p> Shinzi collects and stores your date of birth in your Firebase profile. It may be used for age eligibility checks and related account purposes. </p> <p> Keep your information accurate. Do not enter another person's personal information without appropriate permission. </p> </section> <section> <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2> <p>Information may be used to:</p> <ul> <li>Create, maintain, and authenticate your account.</li> <li>Display and manage your profile.</li> <li>Save profile information and related account records.</li> <li>Enable profile photo selection and upload.</li> <li>Maintain service security and investigate misuse.</li> <li>Respond to support requests and account-related questions.</li> <li>Meet applicable legal obligations.</li> </ul> <p> We do not state that a feature is active merely because it is listed here. Information is used only for purposes supported by the service and applicable law. </p> </section> <section> <h2>5. Firebase and Account Data</h2> <p> Shinzi uses Firebase services for account authentication and profile data. Depending on the feature, this can include Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore. </p> <p> Firebase processes and stores information under the applicable Google service terms and privacy practices. Access to account data should be restricted to authorized systems and personnel. </p> </section> <section> <h2>6. Google Drive and Profile Photos</h2> <p> Shinzi supports profile photo uploads through Google Drive using Google OAuth authorization. When you connect your Google account and choose a photo, Shinzi can use the access granted to perform the relevant file operation. </p> <p> Shinzi may store related file references and metadata in its database so the selected photo can be associated with your profile. </p> <ul> <li> Google account authorization is handled through Google's authorization system. </li> <li> Access is limited by the permissions granted and the functionality Shinzi implements. </li> <li> You can review or revoke Shinzi's Google account access through your Google Account settings. </li> </ul> <p> Revoking access may prevent photo upload or other connected features from working. Revoking Google access does not necessarily delete a photo or its metadata that was previously saved. </p> <p> Google handles information it processes under its own privacy policy. Shinzi does not claim ownership of your Google account or personal photos. </p> </section> <section> <h2>7. Sharing and Third-Party Services</h2> <p> We do not sell your personal information as a business practice. Information may be processed by service providers needed to run Shinzi, including: </p> <ul> <li>Firebase and Google Cloud services for authentication and data.</li> <li>Google Drive and Google OAuth for authorized photo operations.</li> <li>Vercel for website hosting and deployment.</li> </ul> <p> These providers may process information under their own terms, privacy policies, and applicable legal requirements. We may also disclose information when required by law or when reasonably necessary to protect the service, its users, or others. </p> </section> <section> <h2>8. Data Security</h2> <p> We aim to protect account information using appropriate technical and organizational measures. However, no website, online service, or method of electronic storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure. </p> <p> Keep your password private and contact support if you suspect unauthorized access to your account. </p> </section> <section> <h2>9. Data Retention and Account Deletion</h2> <p> We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide Shinzi, maintain account records, address security issues, and meet legal obligations. </p> <p> <strong>Account deletion is currently handled manually through support.</strong> An automated, self-service account deletion feature is not currently offered. </p> <p> To request account and associated data deletion, contact Shinzi using the official support contact published on our website. We may need to verify that the request comes from the account owner before processing it. </p> <p> Deletion requests will be reviewed and processed as applicable. Some information may need to be retained where required by law or for legitimate security purposes. Removing Shinzi's records does not automatically guarantee deletion of files or records held separately by Google or other providers; those may require separate action. </p> </section> <section> <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2> <p> Shinzi is not intended to be used in violation of applicable age requirements or privacy laws. Signup may use date-of-birth information to check age eligibility. </p> <p> If you believe a child has provided personal information in a way that violates applicable requirements, contact support so the situation can be reviewed. </p> </section> <section> <h2>11. Your Choices and Rights</h2> <p> Depending on applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information. You may also manage Google authorization through your Google Account settings. </p> <p> Contact support to submit a privacy request. We may request reasonable verification before acting on it. </p> </section> <section> <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2> <p> We may update this Privacy Policy when Shinzi's features, data practices, or legal obligations change. The latest version will be published on this page with its effective date updated when appropriate. </p> <p> Please review this page periodically to stay informed about our privacy practices. </p> </section> <section> <h2>13. Contact Shinzi</h2> <p> For privacy questions, access requests, corrections, or account deletion requests, contact Shinzi through its official support channel. </p> <p className="privacy-contact-note"> Official support email or contact link: To be added before public release. </p> </section> <footer className="privacy-footer"> <p>© Shinzi. All rights reserved.</p> <p>Privacy matters. Use Shinzi responsibly.</p> </footer> </article> </main> ); } 

